"""
GANTT CHART TEMPLATE  -  STEP PLAN WITH AN EXAMPLE OF EVERY FEATURE
===================================================================
Same engine as gantt_template.py, but the example plan is organised in four phases
(Step 1, Step 2, Cooperation, Step 3) and every feature of the template is used at least once.
Each row in section 1 has a comment starting with "<-" that names the feature it shows.

FEATURE INDEX  (row ids refer to the plan in section 1)
  Building blocks
    G  phase header ........................ "Step 1" ... "Step 3"
    T  task ................................ all s.. and c.. rows
    M  milestone ........................... m1 (no date), m2 (color), m3
    D  deadline ............................ d1 (with time), d2 (date only), d3
    E  fixed date / event .................. e1 (one day), e2 (period)
  Dates of a task
    start + end ............................ s1a, c1
    start + duration ....................... the slides task (id None)
    end + duration (planned backwards) ..... s1d
    dep + duration (auto-scheduled) ........ s1b, s2b, s3a ...
    dep + end .............................. s3c
    dep + fixed dates (arrow only) ......... c2
    id = None (nobody refers to the row) ... the slides task
  Dependencies
    finish-to-start ........................ dep="s1a"
    start-to-start with lag ................ s1c  (dep="s1b:SS+3")
    finish-to-finish ....................... s2c  (dep="s2b:FF")
    negative lag (overlap) ................. s2d  (dep="s2a-2")
    several predecessors ................... m1, s3a
    milestone without a date ............... m1
  Look and extra information
    buffer ................................. s2a, c3
    baseline (original plan) ............... s2a
    ext=True (external dependency) ......... "Cooperation", c1 - c3
    progress (own value / from status) ..... s1b, s1c, c1 / s1a
    color .................................. m2, s3b, "Step 3"
    owner, priority, note .................. almost every row
    status: all five ....................... done s1a, in progress s1b, not started s1d,
                                             at risk s2b, blocked c2
  Phases (G) with their own values ......... "Cooperation": own start / end / progress,
                                             "Step 3": own color, "Step 1": status / note
  Settings ................................. TABLE_COLUMNS (all 7), DATE_FORMAT, TODAY,
                                             SHADE_WEEKENDS, DURATION_IN_WORKDAYS,
                                             TIMELINE_START / END, NON_WORKING (break + single day)
A self-contained template for clean project Gantt charts (matplotlib + pandas).

HOW TO USE
----------
1. Install the requirements once:      pip install pandas matplotlib
2. Edit section "1) YOUR PLAN" below (title, settings, rows).
3. Run:                                python gantt_template_steps.py
   -> the chart is saved as gantt_chart.png (and shown on screen).

BUILDING BLOCKS (used inside `rows`)
------------------------------------
G(name, ...)                        phase / group header (its bar is computed from its tasks)
T(id, name, start, end, ...)        task
M(id, name, date, ...)              milestone  (your own target, drawn as a diamond)
D(id, name, date, ...)              deadline   (fixed by someone else, drawn as a red flag)
E(id, name, start, end, ...)        fixed date / event (seminar, meeting, exam period ...)

Use `None` as id if nobody needs to refer to the row:  T(None, "Write notes", ...)
A row belongs to the phase G(...) above it.

ALL ARGUMENTS
-------------
Dates (all as "YYYY-MM-DD"; the end date is INCLUSIVE; D() also accepts "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM")

    start, end       first and last day
    duration         length in days (or working days, see DURATION_IN_WORKDAYS)
    date             day of a milestone / deadline

    A task needs two of  start / end / duration.  Everything else is derived:
        start + end        -> duration is calculated
        start + duration   -> end is calculated
        end   + duration   -> start is calculated (planning backwards)
        dep   + duration   -> start is calculated from the predecessor (auto-scheduling)
        dep   + end        -> start is calculated from the predecessor
    A milestone without a date takes it from its predecessor (dep).

Links
    dep              predecessor(s), see DEPENDENCIES below
    buffer           days of slack reserved after the task (drawn dashed, auto-scheduled
                     successors start after it)

Look
    ext=True         depends on something outside your control (orange, hatched)
    color="#RRGGBB"  own color for this bar / marker
    progress         0.0 - 1.0, completed share (dark part of the bar). If left out:
                     1.0 for status "done", otherwise 0. Phases are averaged from their tasks.
    baseline         ("YYYY-MM-DD", "YYYY-MM-DD") original plan, drawn as a thin grey bar

Information (shown in the table and/or next to the bar)
    owner            who is responsible, e.g. "AB"
    status           "not started" | "in progress" | "done" | "at risk" | "blocked"
    priority         "high" | "medium" | "low"  (any text works, these three are colored)
    note             short remark shown next to the bar, e.g. "waiting for lab"

DEPENDENCIES
------------
    dep="t1"             finish-to-start: starts the day after t1 ends
    dep="t1:SS"          start-to-start:  starts together with t1
    dep="t1:FF"          finish-to-finish: ends together with t1
    dep="t1:SS+7"        ...with a lag of 7 days  (negative values = overlap, e.g. "t1-2")
    dep=["a", "b:FF"]    several predecessors; the latest one decides the start

SETTINGS
--------
Everything in "SETTINGS" below: title, table columns, language of the labels, status date
("today"), non-working periods (holidays, breaks), weekend shading, working-day durations,
fixed time range, output file and resolution.

RULES OF THUMB
--------------
* Put a task DIRECTLY BELOW its predecessor if you use `dep`; arrows then stay short.
* ids are unique and may contain letters, digits and underscore only.
* If something is wrong with the plan (unknown id, missing dates, circular dependency ...)
  the script stops with a readable message. A dependency that is violated by manually
  entered dates only prints a WARNING.
* The red "Today" marker only appears if the status date lies inside the plan period.
"""

